  "raw_text": "rent things. And I usually get something that is not very expensive. So I stick to things that I've always liked usually. Agent: Thank you for sharing that. What does \"good value\" mean to you in fast food? Could you pick your top two or three factors, such as taste, portion size, speed, nutrition, consistency, or price, and explain how you judge if something is \"worth it\"? User: I like if you go and you get to the fast food restaurant and you get something that is a whole meal. You get the main meal and you get a drink. That's good value. And so that's important. And if you look for set deals, it's like they have buy one, get the other free. That might be something that you look for as well. Agent: That's a clear definition of good value. Now, compared to your last fast-food order, what changed today, if anything? User: Nothing changed that I can think of. The last time I got something, I got the same thing that I usually get and it was good and I paid about the same price, I believe.",
